1
00:00:01,180 --> 00:00:03,060
米奇尔 我是克莱尔 现在是周六早上
Hey, Mitchell. Claire. Saturday morning.

2
00:00:03,120 --> 00:00:04,960
我要你去给妈妈买一份生日礼物
Look, I need you to buy Mom a birthday present

3
00:00:04,960 --> 00:00:06,100
然后说是我们俩合送的
and say it's from the both of us.

4
00:00:06,160 --> 00:00:07,080
就这样 谢谢 拜拜
Okay, thanks. Bye-bye --

5
00:00:07,240 --> 00:00:08,640
我知道这不是语音留言
No, I know it's not a voicemail.

6
00:00:08,700 --> 00:00:10,120
我只是不想听你唧唧歪歪
I just don't want to hear you whine about it.

7
00:00:11,320 --> 00:00:12,840
不行 不行 那些是给艾丽克斯的
No, no, no, those are for Alex.

8
00:00:12,960 --> 00:00:14,320
我今天要送去宿舍给她
I'm taking them up to her dorm today.

9
00:00:14,320 --> 00:00:15,580
你也知道她最近压力多大
You know how stressed she gets.

10
00:00:15,800 --> 00:00:18,740
我想她能随时得到来自母亲的安慰
She can always use a little comfort from her loving mom.

11
00:00:19,580 --> 00:00:21,380
为什么艾丽克斯有爱心包裹 而我却没有
Why does Alex get a care package and not me?

12
00:00:21,600 --> 00:00:22,858
你就住在爱心包裹里
You live in a care package.

13
00:00:22,858 --> 00:00:24,940
海莉 赶紧把人皮画上 到楼上来
Haley, put your face on and get up here!

14
00:00:24,940 --> 00:00:26,000
我们上班要迟到了
We're gonna be late for work!

15
00:00:26,380 --> 00:00:27,960
我最近在存钱给自己买公寓
I'm saving up to get my own apartment,

16
00:00:27,960 --> 00:00:29,777
所以我和卢克一起在俱乐部打工
so I've been working at the club with Luke.

17
00:00:29,777 --> 00:00:31,132
是给卢克打工
For Luke.

18
00:00:31,132 --> 00:00:32,780
这妹子是我手下最赞的球车女郎
Kid's my best cart girl.

19
00:00:32,780 --> 00:00:34,060
我给高尔夫球手送饮料
I deliver drinks to golfers.

20
00:00:34,340 --> 00:00:36,500
小费挺可观 不过 我花了几天
Tips are good, but, uh... it took me a couple days

21
00:00:36,500 --> 00:00:38,140
才领会了这比赛的细枝末节
to learn the finer points of the game.

22
00:00:41,960 --> 00:00:43,040
要鸡尾酒吗 帅哥们
Cocktails, boys?

23
00:00:44,400 --> 00:00:45,500
在你左手边
On your left.

24
00:00:45,700 --> 00:00:47,060
那是艾丽克斯的旧单车吗
Is that Alex's old bike?

25
00:00:47,360 --> 00:00:48,700
是的 重新组装的
Yes, totally rebuilt.

26
00:00:48,800 --> 00:00:51,040
只花了我三个月时间和两管破伤风针
It only took me three months and two tetanus shots.

27
00:00:51,480 --> 00:00:53,540
她最近一直暗示想要辆车
She's been dropping hints about wanting some wheels.

28
00:00:53,880 --> 00:00:55,460
你确定她说的不是...
Are you sure she didn't mean a --

29
00:00:55,460 --> 00:00:57,660
独轮车吗 不 她肯定说了"多轮"车
Unicycle? No. She definitely said "wheels."

30
00:00:57,660 --> 00:01:01,500
车篮正好用来放盥洗用品
Well, the basket's perfect for loading up the toiletries.

31
00:01:01,940 --> 00:01:03,140
还记得我们上次去那里吗
Remember last time we went up there?

32
00:01:03,140 --> 00:01:06,320
她正在用女厕的肥皂粉洗头
She was washing her hair with the powdered soap from the ladies room.

33
00:01:07,700 --> 00:01:10,940
艾丽克斯是个聪明 有学问的...
Alex is an intelligent, accomplished --

34
00:01:10,940 --> 00:01:12,140
-你就直说了吧 -马大哈
- You can just say it. ?- Scatterbrain.

35
00:01:12,420 --> 00:01:14,060
她有时太用功念书
Sometimes, she studies so hard

36
00:01:14,060 --> 00:01:15,580
会忘记一些小事
she forgets about the little things.

37
00:01:16,380 --> 00:01:17,480
我去图书馆
I'll be at the library.

38
00:01:17,840 --> 00:01:19,520
女儿 你是不是忘了什么东西
Uh, honey...aren't you forgetting something?

39
00:01:20,980 --> 00:01:21,980
差点忘了
That was close.

40
00:01:22,220 --> 00:01:22,660
老天
God.

41
00:01:24,180 --> 00:01:25,380
我去处理
I'm on it.

42
00:01:40,660 --> 00:01:43,820
这里就是未来四年我称为"家"的地方
So, this is the place I'll call home for the next four years.

43
00:01:43,840 --> 00:01:45,240
而且因为你念的是戏剧系
And because you're a theater major,

44
00:01:45,340 --> 00:01:47,380
这很可能是你这辈子最大的公寓了
probably the biggest apartment you'll ever have.

45
00:01:47,640 --> 00:01:50,060
在开学第一天 我不想发生两件事
There are two things I want to avoid my first day of school:

46
00:01:50,320 --> 00:01:52,340
被发现我洗完澡穿着滑水鞋出来
getting caught leaving the shower in my aqua shoes,

47
00:01:52,340 --> 00:01:53,840
以及挥泪告别
and a tearful goodbye.

48
00:01:54,260 --> 00:01:56,078
我的同学们始终会看到我哭
My classmates are gonna see me cry eventually.

49
00:01:56,078 --> 00:01:58,140
但我希望是在谢幕的那一刻看见
I'd prefer it be during a curtain call.

50
00:01:58,140 --> 00:01:59,160
我是哥伦比亚人
I am Colombian,

51
00:01:59,400 --> 00:02:02,339
满足曼尼的愿望有违我的天性
so it's against my nature to give Manny what he wants:

52
00:02:02,740 --> 00:02:04,960
他想要冷漠的白人式告别
a cold, white-people goodbye.

53
00:02:06,040 --> 00:02:07,260
但我知道他很多愁善感
But I know he's sensitive,

54
00:02:07,260 --> 00:02:09,640
离家让他很难过
and he's having a hard time leaving the nest,

55
00:02:09,640 --> 00:02:11,160
所以我会顺他的意
so I'm gonna give it to him.

56
00:02:11,440 --> 00:02:12,280
祝你好运 室友
Good luck, chum.

57
00:02:12,560 --> 00:02:14,357
你的浓缩咖啡机想放在哪里
Where do you want your espresso machine?

58
00:02:14,357 --> 00:02:16,160
放我书桌上就行
On my desk is fine.

59
00:02:16,160 --> 00:02:17,200
别担心 特雷弗
And don't worry, Trevor.

60
00:02:17,200 --> 00:02:19,257
买咖啡豆的钱用脏话罐里的罚款付
We'll pay for the beans with the money from our swear jar.

61
00:02:19,257 --> 00:02:22,200
别忘了 四点后不许喝咖啡
Don't forget -- no coffee after 4:00,

62
00:02:22,200 --> 00:02:23,538
否则你会做噩梦
or you get the nightmares.

63
00:02:23,538 --> 00:02:25,683
接下来我自己搞定就行了
I think I can take it from here.

64
00:02:26,560 --> 00:02:28,300
谢谢二位的帮忙
Thank you both for all of your help.

65
00:02:28,500 --> 00:02:28,980
不客气
Sure thing.

66
00:02:29,960 --> 00:02:32,460
我们保持联络 儿子
We will keep in touch, son.

67
00:02:34,760 --> 00:02:36,020
这位朋友
Well, my friend,

68
00:02:36,100 --> 00:02:38,760
你刚刚见证了十分罕见的完美告别
you have just witnessed the rare perfect goodbye.

69
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:41,720
历史上仅记录到过几次完美告别
History records but few flawless farewells:

70
00:02:41,920 --> 00:02:43,700
奥斯卡·王尔德临终之时的珠玑妙语
Oscar Wilde's deathbed bon mot,

71
00:02:44,260 --> 00:02:45,640
白瑞德毫不在乎...
Rhett Butler not giving a --

72
00:02:46,500 --> 00:02:46,900
我靠
Damn it.

73
00:02:47,280 --> 00:02:49,300
我把白噪音机忘在家了
I left my white noise machine at home.

74
00:02:49,640 --> 00:02:50,866
这下我不得不回去
Now I have to go back there,

75
00:02:50,866 --> 00:02:52,260
可能会毁掉我们的完美告别呢
and risk ruining our perfect goodbye.

76
00:02:52,260 --> 00:02:54,260
但你会感谢我的 特雷弗
But you're gonna thank me, Trevor.

77
00:02:54,600 --> 00:02:58,500
持续的背景噪音能安抚...
There's something soothing about constant background noise that...

78
00:02:58,500 --> 00:02:58,940
小特
Trev?

79
00:03:01,440 --> 00:03:03,020
一杯金汤力
One gin and tonic.

80
00:03:03,560 --> 00:03:05,520
希望不是你... 开车[开球]
I hope you're not... driving.

81
00:03:06,860 --> 00:03:09,000
抱歉 这笑话通常高尔夫球手们都很喜欢
Sorry, that's usually a big hit with the golfers.

82
00:03:09,380 --> 00:03:10,300
很好笑
It was hilarious.

83
00:03:10,400 --> 00:03:12,480
但我尽力避免长出笑纹
But I'm trying to avoid laugh lines.

84
00:03:12,780 --> 00:03:13,657
我懂
I get that.

85
00:03:13,657 --> 00:03:16,340
我不想长鱼尾纹 所以我从不眯眼
I don't want crow's feet, so I never squint,

86
00:03:16,340 --> 00:03:19,300
哪怕警察正用手电筒直照我的双眼
even if a cop is shining his flashlight directly in my eyes.

87
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:23,120
我每周一次穿着涂满凡士林的潜水服睡觉
Once a week, I sleep in a wetsuit full of Vaseline.

88
00:03:23,500 --> 00:03:24,400
效果显著啊
It shows.

89
00:03:24,940 --> 00:03:26,860
简直像遇到三十年后的我
It was like meeting myself in 30 years.

90
00:03:27,060 --> 00:03:28,620
原来我真的驻颜有术
Turns out, I really held up.

91
00:03:29,760 --> 00:03:30,880
早上好 拉帕波特女士
Good morning, Ms. Rappaport.

92
00:03:31,520 --> 00:03:32,080
你好
Oh, hello...

93
00:03:32,400 --> 00:03:33,700
-你叫杜克对吧 -是的
- Duke, is it? ?- Yes.

94
00:03:34,260 --> 00:03:35,817
海莉 你是不是该回球车上去了
Haley, shouldn't you be getting back to your cart?

95
00:03:35,817 --> 00:03:37,760
是朗达叫我陪她坐的
Rhonda asked me to sit down.

96
00:03:37,760 --> 00:03:39,660
我们明令禁止员工和会员过于亲密
There's a rule against staff fraternizing with members,

97
00:03:39,660 --> 00:03:41,100
某人伸出脖子上的人头为你担保
and you wouldn't want to make trouble for whoever

98
00:03:41,100 --> 00:03:42,560
推荐你来工作 你要安分
stuck their neck out to get you this job.

99
00:03:42,680 --> 00:03:44,400
多伸伸脖子是好事
Oh, I recommend sticking your neck out.

100
00:03:44,400 --> 00:03:47,380
那是唯一不动刀就能预防双下巴的方法
It's the only nonsurgical way to prevent champagne chin.

101
00:03:47,380 --> 00:03:49,841
-说起来... -我去吧
- Speaking of which, um... - Oh, here. Let me get --

102
00:03:49,841 --> 00:03:51,910
不不不 你坐 让他去
Oh, no, no, no, You sit. He's up.

103
00:03:52,140 --> 00:03:53,620
给我也续一杯吧 杜克
You can top me off, too, Duke.

104
00:03:56,120 --> 00:03:58,269
喝这个果蔬奶昔早餐最赞的是
I am loving this new smoothie kick.

105
00:03:58,269 --> 00:04:00,600
我感觉我今天一天摄入的绿色蔬菜
I-I feel like I've had more green vegetables today

106
00:04:00,600 --> 00:04:01,880
比我爸一辈子摄入得还多
than my dad's had in a lifetime.

107
00:04:02,140 --> 00:04:03,540
我觉得你这新早餐最棒的地方
What I love about your smoothie kick

108
00:04:03,540 --> 00:04:04,920
就是你总念叨个没完
is how much you talk about it.

109
00:04:05,160 --> 00:04:06,580
如果你想损我至少想点有趣的梗
Okay, if you're gonna be mean, be funny.

110
00:04:07,020 --> 00:04:07,880
把车往凸出的路面上推
Aim for the bumps.

111
00:04:08,080 --> 00:04:09,700
卡尔喜欢偶尔颠一颠
Cal likes a bit of a bumpy ride

112
00:04:09,700 --> 00:04:12,560
因为我直到孕期第四阶段还在开拖拉机
on account of I drove a tractor into my fourth trimester.

113
00:04:12,600 --> 00:04:14,181
那声音总让我很不安
Oh, that sound makes me so nervous.

114
00:04:14,181 --> 00:04:17,517
某个可怜的家庭就要天翻地覆了
Some poor family is about to have their life turned upside down.

115
00:04:17,980 --> 00:04:19,500
好像拐到咱家那条街去了
they seem to be turning down our street.

116
00:04:21,800 --> 00:04:24,360
我知道他们都是救火英雄
So, I-I know that they're-they're heroes and all,

117
00:04:24,360 --> 00:04:27,220
但他们会帮我们打扫吗 还是我们自己来
but a-are they sweeping up or is that on us?

118
00:04:27,320 --> 00:04:28,880
你知道吗 我们得一钉一铆
Okay, you know what? We're gonna have to totally rebuild,

119
00:04:28,880 --> 00:04:29,680
彻底重建了
down to the studs.

120
00:04:30,080 --> 00:04:31,000
我要抓狂了
I'm distraught.

121
00:04:31,320 --> 00:04:31,860
是吗
Are ya?

122
00:04:32,660 --> 00:04:35,238
我也不是一口咬定这火是小卡放的
I'm not saying Cam definitely set the fire.

123
00:04:35,238 --> 00:04:37,500
犯人可能是任何一个
It could have been anyone who's spent years

124
00:04:37,500 --> 00:04:40,780
多年来一直在找借口重建厨房的家伙
searching for a way to justify the remodel of our kitchen.

125
00:04:41,060 --> 00:04:43,500
你不是真的在指控我故意放火
Are you actually accusing me of starting this fire

126
00:04:43,500 --> 00:04:45,080
只为了能重建这个丑得要命的厨房吧
just so we could rebuild our hideous kitchen?

127
00:04:45,360 --> 00:04:46,700
指控倒不至于
Uh, accusing, no.

128
00:04:46,700 --> 00:04:48,640
不过你说"丑得要命的厨房"这种话时
but when you say things like "hideous kitchen,"

129
00:04:48,640 --> 00:04:49,860
的确让我有所怀疑
it does make me wonder.

130
00:04:50,160 --> 00:04:51,260
可能是这个引起了火灾
This could be the cause.

131
00:04:51,920 --> 00:04:53,320
大多数厨房失火都是烤箱引起的
Most kitchen fires start in the oven.

132
00:04:53,553 --> 00:04:56,140
我的天哪 我走时没关烤箱吗
Oh, my God, did-did I leave the oven on?

133
00:04:56,140 --> 00:04:58,180
看来我们找到了热腾腾的罪魁祸"包"了
Well, it appears we found our smoking "bun."

134
00:05:00,820 --> 00:05:02,960
她在这住了一夏天 估计是场硬仗
she's been here all summer, so this could be pretty rough.

135
00:05:03,060 --> 00:05:04,960
还记得上次我们在她房间里发现了老鼠吗
Remember last time there was a rat in her room.

136
00:05:04,980 --> 00:05:06,960
她是科学家 她说老鼠是用来做研究的
She's a scientist. She said it was part of a study.

137
00:05:07,080 --> 00:05:09,160
亲爱的 老鼠是在麦片盒里发现的
Honey, it was in a cereal box.

138
00:05:09,420 --> 00:05:11,184
来吧 超能英雄登场
Okay, time to be heroes.

139
00:05:11,184 --> 00:05:13,560
换下脏床单 世界焕然一新
Change a bed sheet, change the world.

140
00:05:13,560 --> 00:05:14,000
没错
That's right.

141
00:05:15,300 --> 00:05:16,780
我都忘了你们两个要来
I completely forgot you guys were coming.

142
00:05:20,380 --> 00:05:21,859
真不好意思
Oh, yeah, I'm so sorry.

143
00:05:21,859 --> 00:05:24,758
我不知道你们要来 袜子没收好
I wasn't expecting you guys, so... sock.

144
00:05:25,280 --> 00:05:26,780
那是我的旧单车吗
Oh, is that my old bike?

145
00:05:26,980 --> 00:05:27,500
没错
Yep!

146
00:05:27,791 --> 00:05:30,020
-为你翻新了 -太棒了
- Spruced it up for you. - That's great.

147
00:05:30,020 --> 00:05:32,100
不过我刚刚买了辆新的
I actually just bought a new one, though.

148
00:05:33,140 --> 00:05:34,700
你可以用那辆当备用零件
Guess you can use that one for parts.

149
00:05:35,420 --> 00:05:38,520
瞧瞧这是什么 电动手套架
What do we have here? An electric mitten holder.

150
00:05:39,107 --> 00:05:41,860
那是我刚建好的猜拳机器人
It's a rock-paper-scissors robot I just built.

151
00:05:41,860 --> 00:05:41,873
什么
What?!

152
00:05:41,873 --> 00:05:44,640
它的传感器能判断你要出什么
Its sensors anticipate your next move.

153
00:05:44,640 --> 00:05:45,755
普通人才会中招
Maybe for civilians.

154
00:05:45,755 --> 00:05:48,984
但我的敏捷手法是受过多年训练的
But I've been trained in the art of sleight of... hand!

155
00:05:49,060 --> 00:05:49,940
终于
At last...

156
00:05:50,420 --> 00:05:51,280
遇到对手了
a worthy opponent.

157
00:05:51,400 --> 00:05:54,560
宝贝 我给你买了些不容易掉渣的零食
Honey, I got you some snacks that don't crumb up quite so easily.

158
00:05:54,600 --> 00:05:56,760
我就给放在这个...
I'll just tuck them away in this...

159
00:05:56,760 --> 00:05:58,740
已经都买好的零食柜里
fully-stocked snack cabinet.

160
00:05:59,200 --> 00:06:00,994
别忘了纸巾和一次性餐盘
Don't forget the paper towels, the paper plates,

161
00:06:00,994 --> 00:06:03,420
和卫生间的... 石头 不可思议
and the toilet -- Rock! How?!

162
00:06:03,420 --> 00:06:06,280
看来你这里一切都井然有序
Seems like you're doing really, really well here.

163
00:06:07,480 --> 00:06:09,600
那好 我得去机器人实验室了
Okay, well, I have to get to the robotics lab.

164
00:06:09,600 --> 00:06:11,480
不过多谢你们过来看我
But, uh, thank you so much for visiting.

165
00:06:11,480 --> 00:06:12,060
宝贝
Oh, honey.

166
00:06:12,980 --> 00:06:14,903
感觉你表现得超棒
You seem to be doing so well.

167
00:06:14,903 --> 00:06:15,640
洗发水
Shampoo.

168
00:06:15,640 --> 00:06:16,957
我们真为你骄傲 艾丽克斯
We're so proud of you, Alex.

169
00:06:16,957 --> 00:06:18,380
不只是因为你建了一个
And not just because you've built

170
00:06:18,380 --> 00:06:20,340
几乎无法战胜的机器人 该死
a nearly unbeatable robot. Damn it!

171
00:06:21,348 --> 00:06:24,760
-好吧 回见了 二位 -拜拜
- Okay, well, uh... bye, you guys. - Bye!

172
00:06:24,760 --> 00:06:26,236
-拜拜 宝贝 -拜拜 宝贝
- Bye, honey. ?- Bye, honey.

173
00:06:26,236 --> 00:06:29,638
她真的开始能独立了
She is really coming into her own, huh?

174
00:06:29,720 --> 00:06:30,660
看我们把她教得多好
Look what we did.

175
00:06:30,760 --> 00:06:32,220
我不确定这都是我们的功劳
I don't know if we can take all the credit.

176
00:06:32,220 --> 00:06:33,720
她来这前不是这样子的
She wasn't like that before she got here.

177
00:06:33,900 --> 00:06:35,140
是我们送她来的 亲爱的
You know what? We drove her here, honey.

178
00:06:35,500 --> 00:06:36,720
是我们送她来的
We drove her here.

179
00:06:37,380 --> 00:06:38,755
谁会需要两罐芥末
Two mustards. No one needs that.

180
00:06:38,755 --> 00:06:41,609
这罐我拿走
We'll just take that one home.

181
00:06:41,660 --> 00:06:43,480
那是她的新裙子
That is her new dress.

182
00:06:44,200 --> 00:06:46,320
她买的时候可兴奋了
She was so excited about getting this.

183
00:06:46,320 --> 00:06:47,338
她为什么要丢掉
Why would she throw it out?

184
00:06:47,338 --> 00:06:48,925
你觉得有什么问题吗
Do you think something's going on?

185
00:06:48,925 --> 00:06:51,161
可能 可能她打扫卫生 整理东西啊
Maybe -- Maybe all of the cleaning and the organizing

186
00:06:51,161 --> 00:06:53,480
都是遭遇困难时的应对机制
is like a -- a coping mechanism.

187
00:06:53,480 --> 00:06:56,100
对 从打扫整理与对自行车的冷漠回应...
Yeah, between that and the muted response to the bike...

188
00:06:56,900 --> 00:06:58,820
我不知道 你觉得我们该找她谈谈吗
I don't know. You think we should talk to her?

189
00:06:59,100 --> 00:07:00,740
我刚都不是在玩
I wasn't even playing.

190
00:07:00,880 --> 00:07:02,260
啊哈 可恶
Boom! Damn it.

191
00:07:02,560 --> 00:07:04,060
被枪抵着 我心中的前三名是
Gun to my head, my top three:

192
00:07:04,220 --> 00:07:05,800
切达奶酪 瑞士硬奶酪 高达奶酪
cheddar, Swiss, gouda.

193
00:07:05,800 --> 00:07:08,799
作为一个真被人拿枪抵着头过的人
As someone who has actually had a gun to her head,

194
00:07:08,799 --> 00:07:11,450
他们才不会问你喜欢什么奶酪
cheese is not what they're going to ask about.

195
00:07:13,300 --> 00:07:14,180
现在到饼干了
And now crackers.

196
00:07:15,800 --> 00:07:16,760
你在干嘛
What are you doing?

197
00:07:17,700 --> 00:07:18,840
尴尬了
This is awkward.

198
00:07:19,780 --> 00:07:21,340
我想改装个爷们天地
I need a boy cave.

199
00:07:21,340 --> 00:07:23,145
别和我提布里奶酪
And don't get me started about brie.

200
00:07:23,145 --> 00:07:24,481
不用担心
Oh, there's no risk of that.

201
00:07:24,481 --> 00:07:26,087
当我没来过 明白吗
I'm not here, okay?

202
00:07:28,540 --> 00:07:30,039
