Not wimp, just soft.

216
00:07:59,580 --> 00:08:00,683
还非常 非常害怕
And very, very scared.

217
00:08:00,683 --> 00:08:02,040
好了 你们能闭嘴了吗
Okay, can everyone please stop talking

218
00:08:02,040 --> 00:08:03,500
这样我们完美的道别还能有点救
so we can salvage our perfect goodbye?

219
00:08:05,400 --> 00:08:06,540
你上锁是干嘛
What's with the padlock?

220
00:08:06,960 --> 00:08:08,160
我问你
Let me ask you something:

221
00:08:08,960 --> 00:08:10,840
你想每天都过圣诞节吗
How would you like to have Christmas every day?

222
00:08:11,525 --> 00:08:14,351
好了 我把我们所需要用的
Okay, I've put everything out here

223
00:08:14,351 --> 00:08:15,685
厨房用品都放到这里了
from the kitchen that we're gonna need.

224
00:08:15,685 --> 00:08:17,200
你知道吗 这会很有趣的
You know what? This is gonna be fun.

225
00:08:17,200 --> 00:08:17,940
就好像露营
It's like camping!

226
00:08:18,200 --> 00:08:19,713
有趣和好像露营并不会同时发生
Which is it -- fun or like camping?

227
00:08:19,713 --> 00:08:21,900
我要去冲个澡
I'm gonna take a shower.

228
00:08:21,900 --> 00:08:23,480
洗澡前先刷了这堆盘子
Can't take a shower without doing a load of dishes.

229
00:08:23,480 --> 00:08:26,500
记得 糙的一边刷锅 软的一边手拿
And remember -- scratchy side pot, soft side you, okay?

230
00:08:26,500 --> 00:08:27,620
小卡 这也太神经病了
Cam, this is crazy.

231
00:08:27,760 --> 00:08:29,580
如果... 如果我想泡杯茶呢
What -- What if I wanted to make a cup of tea?

232
00:08:29,680 --> 00:08:30,403
再简单不过了
Couldn't be simpler.

233
00:08:30,403 --> 00:08:31,920
从餐具柜上拿茶壶
Grab a tea kettle from the credenza,

234
00:08:31,920 --> 00:08:34,420
加水就从窗外接进来的水管加
warm it up on the hot plate with the water that you've used

235
00:08:34,420 --> 00:08:35,970
然后放电炉上热就行了
from the hose that I snaked in through the window,

236
00:08:35,970 --> 00:08:38,959
茶可以去我们壁炉架上找 然后茶杯就在...
browse the tea on the mantel, and then grab our tea cup --

237
00:08:38,959 --> 00:08:42,071
茶杯在... 莉莉 先洗茶杯
Where -- Oh! Lily, do our tea cup first!

238
00:08:42,490 --> 00:08:44,568
你们赶紧把走廊上的冰箱移走
Y'all need to move that 'fridgerator in your hall.

239
00:08:44,568 --> 00:08:46,380
冰箱正好在小卡尔的婴儿床下方
It is straight under little Cal's crib,

240
00:08:46,380 --> 00:08:47,900
冰箱的响声让他一直睡不着
and the noise is keeping him up...

241
00:08:48,260 --> 00:08:50,840
这也怪了 他可是在屠宰场里怀上的啊
which is weird because he was conceived in a slaughterhouse.

242
00:08:50,840 --> 00:08:52,620
-但我还以为... -赶紧移走
- But I thought... - ?Just move it!

243
00:08:52,620 --> 00:08:52,880
你...
You...

244
00:08:54,740 --> 00:08:56,256
他们找到起火的原因了吗
They figure out what started that fire?

245
00:08:56,256 --> 00:08:57,640
嗯 他们认为起因在烤箱
Yeah, they think it was the oven.

246
00:08:57,640 --> 00:08:58,580
不可能
Well, that's dumb.

247
00:08:58,720 --> 00:09:00,960
咱们出去散步前我关了烤箱的
I turned the oven off 'fore we went on our walk.

248
00:09:00,960 --> 00:09:02,499
-你关了吗 -对啊
- You did? - ?Yeah,

249
00:09:02,499 --> 00:09:05,431
因为我是这儿唯一一个有责任心的人
'cause I'm the only responsible person around here.

250
00:09:06,278 --> 00:09:09,678
靠 卡尔又从沙发上滚下来了
Dang it! Cal rolled off the sofa again!

251
00:09:12,520 --> 00:09:14,940
天啊 不 不 不
Oh, God. Oh, no. Oh, no. Oh, no.

252
00:09:17,500 --> 00:09:20,920
有那么一丝可能 凶手绝对是我
There's a small chance I definitely started the fire.

253
00:09:22,597 --> 00:09:24,700
-米奇尔 -奶昔有点稠
- Mitchell? - ?My smoothie was a little thick.

254
00:09:24,700 --> 00:09:25,860
这样还挺方便啊
This is convenient. Huh?

255
00:09:25,860 --> 00:09:27,300
我要给你看点东西
There's something I need to show you.

256
00:09:27,340 --> 00:09:29,180
是什么 来这儿 来这儿看
Yeah. What is it? Over here. Over here. Let's look.

257
00:09:29,180 --> 00:09:30,719
是我梦想厨房的展望板
It's a vision board for my dream kitchen

258
00:09:30,719 --> 00:09:33,150
我一直藏在你的健身服后面
I've been hiding behind your workout clothes. ?Ah.

259
00:09:33,191 --> 00:09:35,511
我觉得我不小心 成心地
I-I-I think I accidentally, on purpose,

260
00:09:35,511 --> 00:09:38,225
下意识地 故意地烧了咱们的厨房
subconsciously, willfully, burned our kitchen down.

261
00:09:38,225 --> 00:09:40,424
我不... 这很难说吧
Okay. I-I don't -- I don't know about that.

262
00:09:40,424 --> 00:09:41,060
不 面对现实吧
Um -- ?No. Let's face it.

263
00:09:41,060 --> 00:09:43,240
就像德鲁·巴里摩尔 我是个可爱的纵火犯
Like Drew Barrymore, I'm an adorable fire starter.

264
00:09:44,100 --> 00:09:45,640
这就是为什么我们家胶布总是没了吗
Is this why we never have any tape?

265
00:09:45,840 --> 00:09:47,922
对 我是个危险人物 所以应该由你
Yes. I'm a menace, which is why you deserve

266
00:09:47,922 --> 00:09:49,961
全权负责这次改造
to be in charge of this entire remodel.

267
00:09:50,160 --> 00:09:51,540
你说了算
Anything you say goes.

268
00:09:52,960 --> 00:09:55,760
小卡 你听完这话感觉会好点的...
Cam, you're about to feel a lot better because

269
00:09:55,760 --> 00:09:58,520
我觉得这烤面包机还行
I don't hate this toaster,

270
00:09:58,520 --> 00:10:00,060
我觉得我能找到位子摆放
and I think I can find a place for it.

271
00:10:00,620 --> 00:10:01,260
太好了
That's great.

272
00:10:02,560 --> 00:10:04,160
我能习惯这种生活
I could get used to this.

273
00:10:04,500 --> 00:10:07,320
我已经习惯了 所以在我亡夫特么的钱
I have, which is why I need to snag another meal ticket

274
00:10:07,320 --> 00:10:09,640
用完之前 我得另找一张饭票
before my late husband's fracking money runs out.

275
00:10:10,020 --> 00:10:11,900
没事 你可以在我面前直接骂脏话
It's okay. You can swear in front of me.

276
00:10:13,820 --> 00:10:16,060
那边那个 在打网球的男人怎么样
How about that guy over there, playing tennis?

277
00:10:16,220 --> 00:10:17,100
他体态挺好
He's in good shape.

278
00:10:17,680 --> 00:10:18,120
对吧
Right?

279
00:10:18,600 --> 00:10:19,480
不 这个不行
No, that's a negative.

280
00:10:19,980 --> 00:10:22,120
我要那种拿网球当助行器缓冲的老头
I want my guys' tennis balls to be at the end of their walkers.

281
00:10:22,120 --> 00:10:24,610
好吧... 那...
Okay. Uh, how about, uh...

282
00:10:24,640 --> 00:10:25,940
那个怎么样
that guy over there?

283
00:10:26,060 --> 00:10:27,820
我想那是个被人丢弃的高尔夫球袋
I think that's just an abandoned golf bag,

284
00:10:27,820 --> 00:10:28,920
不过你开始理解我的意思了
but you're starting to get me.

285
